## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/nightly_red_tracker.sh | ⚠️ important the red night detector only counts conclusion failure — timed out and cancelled red shapes still let the tracker stay closed the self heal decides red night here bash failing gh api repos repo actions runs github run id jobs per page 100 jq jobs select conclusion failure name join two red night job shapes pass this filter as green timed out — the nightly legs carry timeout minutes nightly yml 447 180 493 360 a hung leg killed at its budget concludes timed out not failure cancelled — this repo s own watchdog kills hung jobs and documents that the kill lands as job conclusion cancelled not failure scripts watchdog trip check sh 33 both kill shapes land 82 select conclusion failure or conclusion cancelled fixture shapes in scripts watchdog trip selftest sh 14 17 gh 2290 scripts daily publish report sh 42 likewise counts red as failure or cancelled on such a night the close step still fires step level success — the very mechanism this pr fixes and the self heal then logs decision close stands 1953 — every run leg green no reopen and exits 0 — the tracker stays closed with zero markers i e exactly the 2362 failure mode reintroduced on a subclass of red nights verified against the filter with jq failure → job listed timed out cancelled → empty list → close stands suggested fix bash jq jobs select conclusion failure or conclusion cancelled or conclusion timed out name join plus one such leg in the red run selftest fixture e g conclusion timed out on a needs leg so the shape cannot rot the filer step uses the same narrow filter but there it only renders a job name list — here the same query is the reopen no reopen decision input so under matching changes behavior and repo precedent watchdog trip check sh daily publish report sh already treats failure cancelled as red |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | scripts/nightly_red_tracker.sh | 💡 suggestion the ac2 exhaustion marker dies with the first gh failure — put the human visible comment first the exhaustion path runs under set euo pipefail bash gh label create reopen failed force repo repo aborts the script if it fails gh issue comment number reopen failed manual reopen required gh issue edit number add label reopen failed if gh label create fails e g a github secondary rate limit — plausible right after the reopen→view→reopen burst which is exactly the degraded state ac2 covers the script aborts before the comment and the label land the only remaining signal is the red step and a nonzero exit the issue itself — the thing a human or the fleet sweep looks at — gets nothing which defeats ac2 s loud no sla timer purpose at the moment it matters most consider issuing the tracker comment first then label create gh issue edit or tolerate label create failure with a note label stamp failed fallback so the marker is as robust as the state it reports |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

